Package: bwTools
Type: Package
Title: Native R Tools for BigWig, WIG, and bedGraph Files
Version: 0.8.4
Authors@R: person("Rensc", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "rensc0718@163.com")
Description: Provides native R implementations for reading and writing local
    BigWig files, indexed genomic retrieval, interval statistics, automatic
    multi-track merging, explicit signal aggregation, large-file performance
    benchmarking, and reading and writing WIG and bedGraph signal tracks.
    Version 0.8.0 establishes the downstream-integration stability baseline,
    while 0.8.2 hardens genomic boundary behavior, cross-slot coordinate
    consistency, stable empty query schemas, and chromosome-end handling across
    memory and lazy BigWig modes. Version 0.8.3 aligns scalar retrieval
    validation with the shared genomic interval validator. Version 0.8.4 adds
    an external compatibility validation harness for pyBigWig, rtracklayer,
    and UCSC BigWig utilities without adding runtime dependencies. BigWig
    binary I/O uses base R random-access
    operations, binary encoding, and zlib compression without bundled C or C++
    code or external UCSC executables. Public in-memory signal coordinates are
    1-based closed.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: data.table
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
